      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Bilateral oophorectomy is an essential part in the treatment of gynecologic cancer, and is often performed at the time of hysterectomy to prevent ovarian or/and breast cancer premenopausic women. In our study, we analyzed results from previous reports to determine the influence of estrogen on coronary heart disease, osteoporotic fracture and life expectancy in young patients with medical records of ovarian or breast cancer."},
